Stack as of 2026-10-07, all PRs ready for a reviewer, CI green:
- ENG-2373, PR #1527, commit fc32c8ce3: `packages/database/src/lib/tripleMatching.ts` (NodeTypeIdentity, matchNodeTypes, pickTripleCandidate, parseTripleEndNames, ROAM_DEFAULT_NODE_TYPE_IDS). First written for ENG-2340, isolated per PR guidelines. Child of ENG-2338 (the user said ENG-2328 by mistake). Delegated review: no findings. Loom done.
- ENG-2372, PR #1526, commit bc921e271, base ENG-2373: Obsidian `sourceTriple.ts` (Roam relation schema is already the triple; Obsidian relation matched via pickTripleCandidate), `repairTripleRids.ts` run from `initializeSupabaseSync` before the initial sync, bumps `modified` (scope note: Linear comment a8689730). No match keeps the instance RID, because removing it makes `isAcceptedSchema` treat the triple as local. Delegated review: no findings. Loom shows bug reproduced with a `main` build and repaired (planning vault, local DB, space 169906).
- ENG-2340, PR #1524, base ENG-2373 (see [[eng-2340-roam-relation-import]]).

Facts worth keeping: a triple is a schema, so its RID is `orn:obsidian.schema:<space>/rel3_…`. The planning vault's dev plugin is `.obsidian/plugins/discourse-graph-dev` (symlinked to apps/obsidian/dist); the other `discourse-graphs` folder is easy to confuse. Local DB has the test spaces (22792 planning, 169906, 65215, 170783).

